    {
      "id": "s05",
      "type": "WORKER_SPREAD",
      "transition": "zoom",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "narration": "Sequentially, your hundred tests queue up and go one at a time. Ten minutes twelve. But hand them to four workers and they get dealt out — a quarter each, roughly, running at the same moment in four separate browsers. Two minutes forty-one. Now, nothing got faster here. Not one test. The work just stopped queuing. And the only reason that's allowed is the thing from episode eight — every test gets its own fresh context, so there's nothing to fight over.",
      "data": {
