      "narration": "Which is the bit I genuinely love. A build goes red at three in the morning on a machine you've never seen. Normally you'd get a stack trace and a shrug. Instead, you download trace dot zip from the run, open it with show-trace, and you're standing inside that failure — every step, the page exactly as it looked, the console, the network. On a machine that no longer exists.",
