      "id": "s19",
      "type": "RECAP",
      "transition": "fade",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "narration": "Four lines to take away. Dash n spreads the work across workers, and nothing actually got faster. That only works because your tests are isolated. A test that depends on another test is a coin flip, not a bug. And CI runs the lot on every push, keeping a trace of anything that broke.",
      "data": {
        "heading": "Parallel and CI, in four lines",
        "points": [
          {
            "text": "-n spreads the work. nothing got faster.",
            "atWord": 9.167
          },
          {
            "text": "it is only legal because tests are isolated",
            "atWord": 17.333
          },
          {
            "text": "a chained test is a coin flip, not a bug",
            "atWord": 24.667
          },
          {
            "text": "CI: --with-deps, -n auto, keep the trace",
            "atWord": 30.417
          }
        ]
